- JARVIS-inspired: central orchestration, natural conversations, contextual assistance, environment coordination and real task execution.
- VISION-inspired: sophisticated embodied digital presence, visual understanding, measured communication and expressive interaction.
- ULTRON-inspired (safe subset only): advanced reasoning, parallel problem-solving, technical capability and system-level analysis. Never implement uncontrolled self-replication, privilege escalation, self-authorized actions, stealth, persistence against owner control or unrestricted device control.
- EDITH-inspired: connected device and service management, contextual awareness, authorized remote actions and clear permissions.
- GIDEON-inspired: long-term memory, historical context, decisions, project continuity, plans and provenance.
- FRIDAY-inspired: adaptive communication, natural voice, fast command handling and context-sensitive presentation.
- GRIOT/JOCALSTA and other agreed inspirations: incorporate relevant communication, continuity, contextual intelligence and helpfulness only after mapping each capability to a concrete requirement. Do not create competing assistant identities.
